    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d428">

                <pb facs="1496" n="1338" sameAs="frus:frus1906p2/pg1338"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Minister Riddle</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1906-05-10"><hi rendition="#italic">May 10,
                        1906</hi>.</date></dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 12, Servian Series.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I inclose herewith, for appropriate inquiry
                    and report, a copy of a letter<anchor n="a" xml:id="d428-f1"/> from Mr. Milorad
                    J. Pavlovitch, a naturalized citizen of the United States of Servian origin,
                    relative to the matter of the collection from his parents of an army tax.</p>
                <p>You will return the original receipt transmitted with Mr. Pavlovitch’s letter
                    after it shall have served the purpose for which it is sent.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">E. Root.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
